{"new_lineages":[{"id":"L-spec-faster-than-use","scope":"method","statement":"The specification moves faster than any use, so no program built on Luthier can stabilize."},{"id":"L-luthier-costs-more-than-returns","scope":"method","statement":"As a design Luthier improved this week, but as a sonolocalización tool it today costs the project more than it returns."},{"id":"L-gen-over-refined-type","scope":"language","statement":"A generator is defined only over a type with a predicate, so a type like BrokenGraph must be a refinement subtype whose predicate the generated values are checked against."},{"id":"L-hash-compared-after-holes-filled","scope":"language","statement":"Certificate hashes are compared at the end of loading with the holes filled, a library with holes being a structure with parameters whose laws are certified per filling."},{"id":"L-soundness-regression-suite","scope":"method","statement":"A tests/soundness suite turns today's reproducible failures into regression tests."},{"id":"L-report-statistic-not-block","scope":"method","statement":"A result like a residual's uniformity should be reported as a question, a statistic and its null level, informing rather than blocking (figures with a head)."},{"id":"L-classify-problems-int-spec-proy","scope":"method","statement":"Problems are split into three kinds marked so they don't mix: interpreter, specification and project."},{"id":"L-generated-value-checked-against-type","scope":"language","statement":"Each value a registered generator produces is checked against its type and a value outside it is an error, with gen T trusted as the declared-trust escape."},{"id":"L-materialization-cache-bug","scope":"language","statement":"The materialization cache keyed only by id(f) returns incorrect results, a correctness bug not a performance one."},{"id":"L-vacuous-cases-pass","scope":"language","statement":"Vacuous cases count as passes: an unreached antecedent, a false law with n=0, and an empty exhaustive domain all pass."},{"id":"L-conversion-syntactic-no-dependent-elim","scope":"language","statement":"Conversion is syntactic on neutral terms and there is no dependent elimination, so a type error becomes a pending obligation."},{"id":"L-function-generators-degenerate","scope":"language","statement":"Function generators are degenerate, so any law quantified over functions is tested on a degenerate sample."},{"id":"L-positional-identity-trap","scope":"language","statement":"The positional identity of products and sums lets fields be swapped silently, which the spec says and which is a trap."},{"id":"L-hardwired-names-interpreter","scope":"language","statement":"There are hardwired names in the interpreter, so Fin is recognized only by name and an alias of Fin loses its array representation and memoization."},{"id":"L-preconditions-only-bool-match","scope":"language","statement":"Preconditions are only generated in match over Bool; match by constructor or label generates none."},{"id":"L-one-generator-per-type","scope":"language","statement":"A generator written over an alias is the generator of the type the alias names, and two generators for the same type are an error."},{"id":"L-likelihood-tangent-dimension","scope":"language","statement":"Likelihood does not carry the dimension of its tangent space, so a density pair declared over the whole vector asserted something false and is restated over the dimensioned domain."},{"id":"L-certification-performance-fixes","scope":"language","statement":"Verifying each generated value used the slow substitution evaluator; Bool predicates are now decided on the fast machine and a law's type inferred once per type."},{"id":"L-no-project-python-scripts","scope":"method","statement":"Luthier's intent is that Luciano write no project-dedicated Python except the functions called through extern, and he asks whether the work is making patches."},{"id":"L-name-the-patches","scope":"method","statement":"The patches made in the work should be named as patches and noted in the plan rather than passing as specification."},{"id":"L-lm-controls-excluded","scope":"method","statement":"The Levenberg-Marquardt controls were excluded on purpose because they belong to this particular case."},{"id":"L-interpreter-hash-recertify-cost","scope":"language","statement":"Including the interpreter's fingerprint in the hash means any interpreter fix invalidates every certificate, forcing recertification in batches."},{"id":"L-report-not-decidable","scope":"language","statement":"When the checker cannot read which labels a law touches or decide an equality, it should report not decidable rather than approximate or count all labels as touched."},{"id":"L-implicit-type-params","scope":"language","statement":"Implicit type parameters are deduced by unification at application, so an unannotated lambda is checked after deducing its type from the other argument."},{"id":"L-brokentext-needs-grammar","scope":"language","statement":"Giving BrokenText an honest predicate requires the format's grammar written in Luthier, which today only the Python parser has."},{"id":"L-indexat-nat","scope":"language","statement":"An index typed Int admits negatives and makes an obligation genuinely false, so the honest type for an index is Nat."},{"id":"L-refinements-in-sums-checked-flag","scope":"language","statement":"Refinements inside sums and the --checked flag are added and recorded in the specification."},{"id":"L-time-per-law","scope":"language","statement":"The time each law takes is recorded in its result and in the certificate so the explosive laws can be found."}],
